{"block_id": "0a27c3bc190a_text_0044", "doc_id": "0a27c3bc190a", "company": "AAPL", "fiscal_year": "2024", "page": 1, "section": "The Company’s services also face substantial compe", "block_type": "text", "block_index": 44, "bbox": null, "content_stats": {"char_count": 508, "word_count": 71, "line_count": 3}, "source_path": "data/raw/pdfs/sec-edgar-filings/AAPL/10-K/0000320193-24-000123/primary-document.html", "extraction_method": "automated", "confidence": 0.95, "timestamp": "2025-11-30T11:51:37.327762", "text": "The Company’s business, results of operations and financial condition depend substantially on the Company’s ability to continually improve its products and services to maintain their functional and design advantages. There can be no assurance the Company will be able to continue to provide products and services that compete effectively.\nBusiness Risks\nTo remain competitive and stimulate customer demand, the Company must successfully manage frequent introductions and transitions of products and services.", "full_text_available": true}
